#X text 295 230 If a note-off message arrives \, record the fact that
there are no notes currently sounding.;
#X text 296 267 This assumes that all notes are off as soon as a note-off
message - for any note - is received. This assumption is wrong if you
send all MIDI notes through this object. If two notes are played \,
and only one is released \, then this will still be treated as meaning
that all notes are off.;
#X text 296 345 To avoid this \, pass the MIDI notes through a [monom]
object before sending them to this object.;
